    for the bundled code's licenses.
Description: The 'webR' (<https://docs.r-wasm.org/webr/>) project runs R in a
    web browser through 'WebAssembly'. This package turns a folder of R
    scripts, data files and package names into a static web site that opens an
    in-browser workspace (editor, console, files, plots and environment) with
    those packages and files already in place, and previews it locally. Sites
    deploy to 'GitHub Pages', 'Netlify' or any static host and can be built to
    run fully offline; collection_mirror() builds a self-contained 'webR' site
    and package repository for networks without internet access. Local and
    'GitHub' packages are compiled to 'WebAssembly' with 'Docker'.
License: AGPL-3
URL: https://coatless-wasm.github.io/webrarian/,
    https://github.com/coatless-wasm/webrarian
